-q
----------------------------------------------------------------------
10 CLS
' The values of RND taken from the real BASIC Vilnius. They are the same on
' every run, so they can be compared with the constants below.
' The values are compared with a tolerance: the constants are written with
' 7 digits, and a Single keeps about that many, so the last digit may differ.
'NOTE: the properties of the sequence are checked in 0731-rnd-seq
' The first three values with the default starting state. These lines have to
' go before any RND with a negative argument, such a call replaces the state.
20 A = RND(1)
30 PRINT ".8672345", A
40 B = RND(1)
50 PRINT ".6855049", B
60 C = RND(1)
70 PRINT ".3079186", C
80 B% = ABS(A - 0.8672345) < 0.000001
90 PRINT "-1", B%
100 B% = ABS(B - 0.6855049) < 0.000001
110 PRINT "-1", B%
120 B% = ABS(C - 0.3079186) < 0.000001
130 PRINT "-1", B%
' RND with a negative argument returns a value too, and restarts the sequence:
' PRINT RND(-1) gives .9642279, then two PRINT RND(1) give .1955422, .6406122
140 A = RND(-1)
150 PRINT ".9642279", A
160 B = RND(1)
170 PRINT ".1955422", B
180 C = RND(1)
190 PRINT ".6406122", C
200 B% = ABS(A - 0.9642279) < 0.000001
210 PRINT "-1", B%
220 B% = ABS(B - 0.1955422) < 0.000001
230 PRINT "-1", B%
240 B% = ABS(C - 0.6406122) < 0.000001
250 PRINT "-1", B%
